comments:
Hey @dprov I have raised a PR to fix this
Thanks for the report @dprov. It was done for `RocCurveDisplay` because there was an inconsistency between `RocCurveDisplay.from_predictions` and the function `roc_curve`, see https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/issues/29823. `DetCurveDisplay` has the same inconsistency so I agree that we should change it. Looking at other displays for binary classif, I found that `PrecisionRecallDisplay` is also inconsistent.
Hi @jeremiedbb , I did see that `PrecisionRecallDisplay ` had that inconsistency as well. However because the docstring mentioned only estimated probabilities - contrary to `RocCurveDisplay` and `DetCurveDisplay ` who mention non-thresholded measure of decisions - I thought it made snese to keep it like that. Please let me know if it something I should add to my PR. 
@luiser1401, ``PrecisionRecallDisplay`` mentions "Estimated probabilities or output of decision function." and `precision_recall_curve` has a `y_score` parameter so we should make it consistent as well. It can be done in your existing PR or a separate one, as you prefer.
@jeremiedbb will do it in the existing PR

@jeremiedbb all done now, could you review my PR please? #31764
